index 9f376a1..48df5eb 100644
--- a/docs/templates.rst
+++ b/docs/templates.rst
@@ -1025,6 +1025,59 @@ Filters that accept arguments can be called like this::
 
     {% filter center(100) %}Center this{% endfilter %}
 
+.. _match-statement:
+
+Match
+~~~~~
+
+.. versionadded:: 3.2
+
+``match`` compares a value against a list of patterns, modelled on
+Python's structural pattern matching.  The first ``case`` whose pattern
+matches, and whose optional ``if`` guard is true, is rendered::
+
+    {% match event %}
+      {% case {"type": "login", "user": {"name": name}} %}
+        {{ name }} logged in
+      {% case [first, *rest] if rest %}
+        {{ first }} and {{ rest|length }} more
+      {% case is string as text %}
+        note: {{ text }}
+      {% case _ %}
+        unknown event
+    {% endmatch %}
+
+Only whitespace and comments may appear before the first ``case``.  The
+subject is evaluated once; if no case matches nothing is rendered.
+
+Patterns:
+
+``_``
+    Matches anything.
+``name``
+    Matches anything and binds it to ``name``.
+literals, ``-1``, ``"text"``, ``1.5``
+    Match values equal to the literal.  ``none``, ``true`` and ``false``
+    match by identity.
+dotted names, ``colors.RED``
+    Match values equal to the attribute, looked up like ``{{ colors.RED }}``.
+``[p, *rest]``, ``(p, q)``, ``p, q``
+    Match sequences other than strings and bytes.  ``*rest`` binds the
+    remaining items as a list, ``*_`` ignores them.
+``{"key": p, **rest}``
+    Match mappings containing the keys.  ``**rest`` binds the other items
+    as a dict.
+``p | q``
+    Matches if either alternative matches.  Both must bind the same names.
+``p as name``
+    Binds the value matched by ``p`` to ``name``.
+``is test``, ``is test(args)``, ``is not test``
+    Match if the :ref:`test <tests>` passes, or fails with ``not``.
+
+Each case is a scope of its own, like ``with``: names
+bound by the pattern and variables set in the body are not visible after
+``endmatch``.
+
